1
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:31,440
Overseeing Line Two.

2
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:32,159
Chief Engineer Chen!

3
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,119
Chief Engineer Chen is here!

4
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:33,840
He's here, he's here.

5
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:34,320
I see him.

6
00:00:34,479 --> 00:00:35,119
Chief Engineer Chen is here!

7
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:36,200
Chief Engineer Chen!

8
00:00:37,719 --> 00:00:38,479
He's here! Chief Engineer Chen's here!

9
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:39,280
Here he comes, here he comes!

10
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:40,000
Quick, quick, quick!

11
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:41,359
Chunyan, Chunyan!

12
00:00:41,479 --> 00:00:42,240
Chief Engineer Chen is here!

13
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:42,960
Hurry!

14
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:45,079
Chief Engineer Chen!

15
00:00:45,399 --> 00:00:45,840
Chief Engineer Chen!

16
00:00:46,679 --> 00:00:47,200
You're all here!

17
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:48,479
Have a seat, sit down.

18
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:48,880
Here.

19
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:51,359
Thanks.

20
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:51,960
Stop cracking seeds.

21
00:00:52,359 --> 00:00:53,799
You even brought me a cup.

22
00:00:54,759 --> 00:00:55,320
Stop cracking seeds. Thanks.

23
00:00:55,399 --> 00:00:55,880
Chunyan!

24
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,240
Let's hear Chief Engineer Chen say a few words.

25
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:00,479
Well...

26
00:01:01,359 --> 00:01:02,000
Earlier,

27
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:05,159
I went to Ma Guowen

28
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:06,400
to sound him out...

29
00:01:12,599 --> 00:01:13,079
No, no, no.

30
00:01:13,079 --> 00:01:13,959
He's one of us, one of us.

31
00:01:14,599 --> 00:01:15,319
Keep on recording.

32
00:01:18,079 --> 00:01:19,280
I went to Ma Guowen

33
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:20,319
and felt him out.

34
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:21,599
Know your opponent, right?

35
00:01:21,719 --> 00:01:22,319
Right, right, right!

36
00:01:22,319 --> 00:01:22,840
Isn't that right?

37
00:01:23,239 --> 00:01:24,519
So don't worry, everyone.

38
00:01:25,239 --> 00:01:27,200
On the day of the auction,

39
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:28,560
Qian Yichuan and I

40
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,040
will represent us at the bidding.

41
00:01:31,359 --> 00:01:31,760
Sounds good.

42
00:01:31,799 --> 00:01:32,439
Good, good, good!

43
00:01:32,519 --> 00:01:32,840
Great!

44
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:33,519
Great, wonderful!

45
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:37,319
What I mean is,

46
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:40,439
the spirit of daring to think and act

47
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:42,400
is what Lacheng Brewery is all about!

48
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:43,640
Exactly! That's right!

49
00:01:43,959 --> 00:01:44,560
Right, right, right!

50
00:01:44,599 --> 00:01:45,000
Isn't that so?

51
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,120
Come on, come on!

52
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,280
Let's give Chief Engineer Chen a big hand!

53
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:49,959
All right, that's enough, that's enough.

54
00:01:50,079 --> 00:01:51,079
Have some melon seeds, come on.

55
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,400
Have some seeds, eat up.

56
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:53,239
Here, Chief Engineer Chen.

57
00:01:53,359 --> 00:01:54,239
Have some seeds, help yourself.

58
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,159
Thank you, everyone. Give me a bit more.

59
00:01:55,159 --> 00:01:56,000
That's plenty, that's plenty!

60
00:01:56,359 --> 00:01:57,640
Don't just eat melon seeds.

61
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:58,480
Drink some water.

62
00:01:58,599 --> 00:01:59,200
It dries out your mouth.

63
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:00,040
Have some seeds, don't be shy.

64
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:00,599
Have some seeds.

65
00:02:01,359 --> 00:02:02,159
Have some seeds, eat up.

66
00:02:02,319 --> 00:02:03,120
Have some seeds, have some seeds.

67
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:03,840
Have some seeds.

68
00:02:05,079 --> 00:02:06,120
Why're you handing me empty shells?

69
00:02:07,079 --> 00:02:07,760
I'll get a sore throat!

70
00:02:08,919 --> 00:02:09,599
Eating too many gives you a sore throat.

71
00:03:45,719 --> 00:03:46,879
Where were you the day Cao Jun died?

72
00:03:47,199 --> 00:03:47,879
Cao Jun?

73
00:03:53,639 --> 00:03:54,800
I was at my son's place.

74
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:58,000
Then I had a few drinks,

75
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,240
and slept for a bit.

76
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,759
Later, I drove home.

77
00:04:02,879 --> 00:04:04,759
But as I passed the factory gate,

78
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,199
I hit that sculpture.

79
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:09,919
Then... Then I went to...

80
00:04:11,319 --> 00:04:12,000
the traffic police.

81
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:13,080
Got it all sorted out.

82
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:13,680
Yeah.

83
00:04:15,039 --> 00:04:16,920
I've... I've still got the ticket right here.

84
00:04:18,199 --> 00:04:18,920
Take a look.

85
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:37,959
Wu,

86
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,480
stay with Engineer Chen.

87
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:40,560
Got it. I'll go...

88
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:41,959
verify the ticket.

89
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:43,680
Hurry it up.

90
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:44,720
I need to get home.

91
00:04:54,199 --> 00:04:55,800
Would you keep a ticket forever?

92
00:04:56,439 --> 00:04:57,399
Like a souvenir?

93
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,759
Commemorating...

94
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,079
getting fined?

95
00:05:02,279 --> 00:05:03,920
Carrying it in your wallet every day,

96
00:05:04,839 --> 00:05:05,920
ready to pull it out anytime,

97
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,079
like he's just waiting for me to ask.

98
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:11,360
A ticket isn't a bankbook!

99
00:05:18,519 --> 00:05:19,959
Why isn't he back yet?

100
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:22,839
Officer,

101
00:05:23,399 --> 00:05:24,759
when can I leave?

102
00:05:29,199 --> 00:05:29,839
How about this?

103
00:05:30,399 --> 00:05:32,040
Go get your boss for me.

104
00:05:33,079 --> 00:05:34,519
I have things to deal with at home.

105
00:05:43,399 --> 00:05:44,519
Can I get some water?

106
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:45,959
Cold or hot?

107
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,199
I'll pour some for you.

108
00:05:47,879 --> 00:05:48,680
Oh, so you can talk?

109
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:49,720
Warm.

110
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:54,319
Chief Engineer Chen,

111
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,040
we checked everything out.

112
00:05:56,199 --> 00:05:57,120
Thanks for your cooperation.

113
00:05:57,759 --> 00:05:59,199
The paperwork is all clear.

114
00:05:59,279 --> 00:05:59,959
It's sorted out?

115
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,720
Can I leave now?

116
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:05,680
Just a moment longer.

117
00:06:05,879 --> 00:06:08,519
Didn't you say you hit that sculpture?

118
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,959
Right now, I need you to...

119
00:06:10,959 --> 00:06:12,879
walk me through the details.

120
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,079
How did you hit it?

121
00:06:14,079 --> 00:06:15,120
Why did you hit it?

122
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:16,000
What time did it happen?

123
00:06:16,199 --> 00:06:18,000
Haven't you looked into that already?

124
00:06:18,279 --> 00:06:21,040
Traffic police already settled this.

125
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:22,720
Why are you people...

126
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:23,720
When did you crash?

127
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:24,720
What time?

128
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,319
The middle of the night.

129
00:06:31,399 --> 00:06:32,560
Around 2:00 a.m.

130
00:06:32,839 --> 00:06:34,720
Out joyriding at 2:00 a.m.?

131
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:36,600
Didn't I tell you?

132
00:06:37,079 --> 00:06:38,439
I was at my son's place.

133
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:42,160
I was heading home from there to sleep.

134
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:43,199
Then...

135
00:06:43,519 --> 00:06:44,800
with such a huge sculpture,

136
00:06:45,079 --> 00:06:46,040
how did you manage to hit it?

137
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,040
Couldn't you see it?

138
00:06:47,279 --> 00:06:48,879
A truck was coming toward me.

139
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:49,959
High beams blazing.

140
00:06:49,959 --> 00:06:51,920
Blinded me completely!

141
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,319
So I swerved the wheel,

142
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:53,839
BAM!

143
00:06:53,959 --> 00:06:54,600
Crashed right into it.

144
00:06:54,839 --> 00:06:55,560
Blinded you, huh?

145
00:06:55,759 --> 00:06:57,720
Did you turn this way at the west junction,

146
00:06:57,720 --> 00:06:58,680
or at the east junction

147
00:06:58,720 --> 00:06:59,399
when you turned that way and crashed?

148
00:06:59,399 --> 00:06:59,800
The east one.

149
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,759
Go check it yourself!

150
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:03,759
You're picking on me on purpose!

151
00:07:03,759 --> 00:07:04,480
Let me tell you,

152
00:07:10,439 --> 00:07:11,480
when are you letting me go?

153
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:13,160
If not,

154
00:07:13,199 --> 00:07:14,240
get your boss in here!

155
00:07:14,639 --> 00:07:16,160
I'm just waiting for you to remember.

156
00:07:16,319 --> 00:07:17,240
About the steering wheel...

157
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,279
You remember taking a leak back in '99,

158
00:07:19,319 --> 00:07:20,600
but you forgot how you crashed?

159
00:07:23,519 --> 00:07:24,279
I get it now.

160
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:26,040
That fat guy...

161
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:27,480
you put him up to this, didn't you?

162
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:29,360
Set a trap for me,

163
00:07:29,399 --> 00:07:30,560
brought me here,

164
00:07:30,759 --> 00:07:32,040
and now you're grilling me.

165
00:07:35,839 --> 00:07:36,360
I'm leaving!

166
00:07:37,519 --> 00:07:38,079
Please, sit down.

167
00:07:39,199 --> 00:07:39,800
We're not done talking yet.

168
00:07:40,399 --> 00:07:40,959
Sit down!

169
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,879
Did you hit that sculpture?

170
00:08:07,759 --> 00:08:09,160
You actually believe Chen Qingchun?

171
00:08:10,199 --> 00:08:11,120
I don't!

172
00:08:11,839 --> 00:08:13,279
The guy's got an alibi.

173
00:08:13,519 --> 00:08:15,839
Even if he claimed he hit it sleepwalking,

174
00:08:15,839 --> 00:08:16,439
you'd still have to believe him.

175
00:08:16,879 --> 00:08:17,519
If you want to question him,

176
00:08:17,519 --> 00:08:18,240
you need evidence.

177
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:22,519
Didn't you find any surveillance,

178
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:24,240
any fingerprints,

179
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:26,319
or any leads like that?

180
00:08:27,879 --> 00:08:29,399
If I had even one of those,

181
00:08:29,839 --> 00:08:30,600
I wouldn't be here.

182
00:08:33,399 --> 00:08:34,200
How long has he been locked up?

183
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:37,960
Five or six hours.

184
00:08:39,039 --> 00:08:39,960
Alright, stop taking photos.

185
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:47,000
Cai,

186
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,399
hurry up right now

187
00:08:48,399 --> 00:08:49,639
and check all the repair shops

188
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:50,759
across Lacheng

189
00:08:50,759 --> 00:08:52,639
for records from the past two weeks.

190
00:08:52,759 --> 00:08:54,200
Report back to me when you're done.

191
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:57,679
You,

192
00:08:57,919 --> 00:08:58,600
head to traffic police.

193
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:04,279
Go on!

194
00:09:04,279 --> 00:09:05,120
What are you staring at me for?

195
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:05,879
Where are you going?

196
00:09:06,759 --> 00:09:08,000
Mind your own business.

197
00:09:08,519 --> 00:09:09,639
Then what am I going there for?

198
00:09:10,159 --> 00:09:11,120
Do what you're supposed to do.

199
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:12,080
Do what, exactly?

200
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,639
You do whatever I tell you to do!

201
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:17,559
What're you getting worked up for?

202
00:09:19,639 --> 00:09:20,399
Bring it back to me.

203
00:09:20,879 --> 00:09:21,919
What are you doing?

204
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:24,279
Fine, I'll do whatever you say.

205
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:29,159
Someone crashed into the sculpture.

206
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,480
It was hit right here.

207
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:30,919
Look.

208
00:09:30,919 --> 00:09:31,679
Take a look here.

209
00:09:32,159 --> 00:09:32,679
Who hit it?

210
00:09:33,799 --> 00:09:35,279
Our factory's former chief engineer.

211
00:09:35,399 --> 00:09:36,559
Name's Chen Qingchun.

212
00:09:49,759 --> 00:09:50,399
Brother Chuang,

213
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:52,440
this is Chen Qingchun's car.

214
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:47,000
Gao,

215
00:10:47,399 --> 00:10:48,559
did you get to traffic police yet?

216
00:10:49,799 --> 00:10:51,720
I'm by the sculpture outside Lacheng Brewery.

217
00:10:52,639 --> 00:10:53,720
I found a lead.

218
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:57,720
I picked up a piece of car debris.

219
00:10:58,759 --> 00:11:00,159
But it's silver.

220
00:11:00,799 --> 00:11:02,600
Chen Qingchun's car is black, right?

221
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:06,879
Besides, looking at

222
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,279
where it hit,

223
00:11:09,559 --> 00:11:11,960
it doesn't look like a sedan could reach that high.

224
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:13,120
Two weeks ago,

225
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,039
the sculpture outside Lacheng Brewery's main gate

226
00:11:15,159 --> 00:11:16,080
was struck by a vehicle.

227
00:11:16,559 --> 00:11:17,559
Currently, our city is in

228
00:11:17,559 --> 00:11:18,759
a critical period of

229
00:11:18,759 --> 00:11:19,399
our Civilized City campaign.

230
00:11:19,919 --> 00:11:21,399
This incident has had an egregious impact.

231
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:23,159
If the perpetrator turns themselves in

232
00:11:23,159 --> 00:11:25,039
to the Lacheng Traffic Police Brigade today

233
00:11:25,039 --> 00:11:25,679
and admits responsibility,

234
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,960
leniency may be granted.

235
00:11:27,399 --> 00:11:28,559
Any citizen who comes forward with information

236
00:11:28,559 --> 00:11:29,759
will also be rewarded accordingly.

237
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:55,600
Hello? What's up?

238
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:57,720
Ermao?

239
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:00,080
I... I...

240
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:01,279
I... I...

241
00:12:01,279 --> 00:12:02,159
I wanted to ask...

242
00:12:02,279 --> 00:12:04,000
Isn't Engineer Chen playing cards with you guys?

243
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:05,559
Nope.

244
00:12:05,759 --> 00:12:06,240
He didn't come.

245
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:06,799
He didn't?

246
00:12:07,559 --> 00:12:07,919
Well...

247
00:12:08,279 --> 00:12:10,360
Doesn't he join you guys every day?

248
00:12:10,879 --> 00:12:11,879
Well, he didn't come today.

249
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,320
I tried calling him...

250
00:12:15,519 --> 00:12:16,480
and he didn't pick up.

251
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:18,840
I've been calling him all day too.

252
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:19,679
Can't reach him anywhere.

253
00:12:20,679 --> 00:12:21,080
Really.

254
00:12:22,879 --> 00:12:24,360
Well... you guys carry on then.

255
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:55,480
Tieping,

256
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:57,600
come home at noon.

257
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,039
I have something urgent.

258
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:02,000
Need to go to the traffic police.

259
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:05,279
I just...

260
00:13:05,399 --> 00:13:06,720
My mind went completely blank.

261
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:07,799
I looked up,

262
00:13:07,879 --> 00:13:09,080
and that dark sculpture

263
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:09,799
was right in front of me!

264
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:12,000
I yanked the wheel as hard as I could,

265
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,200
yanked, and then—crash!

266
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:14,639
Alright.

267
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:15,360
In short,

268
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:16,279
you crashed into it, right?

269
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:17,720
Yes, yes, yes.

270
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,519
I really did hit it.

271
00:13:20,519 --> 00:13:21,320
Officer,

272
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,200
I'll take whatever punishment.

273
00:13:24,559 --> 00:13:24,960
I accept it.

274
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:25,440
Sir,

275
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:27,919
you...

276
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:29,279
Why weren't you asleep in the middle of the night?

277
00:13:29,759 --> 00:13:31,000
What were you running off to the factory for?

278
00:13:32,919 --> 00:13:34,360
Isn't the factory about to be sold?

279
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,120
Well,

280
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:37,720
I made plans with a few old buddies

281
00:13:38,159 --> 00:13:39,720
to go back to the factory and chat with them.

282
00:13:41,559 --> 00:13:42,279
You'd been drinking, hadn't you?

283
00:13:42,879 --> 00:13:43,679
No, I hadn't.

284
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,080
Why don't you believe me?

285
00:13:50,559 --> 00:13:51,759
Ever since leaving the factory,

286
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:52,879
I haven't had a drop.

287
00:13:53,759 --> 00:13:54,720
If you weren't drinking,

288
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:55,639
why did you run?

289
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,240
Instead of reporting it to traffic police,

290
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:58,360
you... you just took off?

291
00:13:59,639 --> 00:14:01,279
I didn't think that much.

292
00:14:01,399 --> 00:14:02,279
I just figured,

293
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:03,559
wasn't it...

294
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:05,440
nobody got hurt,

295
00:14:05,639 --> 00:14:06,639
wasn't it just a sculpture?

296
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,240
The factory is being sold anyway.

297
00:14:08,879 --> 00:14:10,000
I'd just spend some money,

298
00:14:10,279 --> 00:14:11,879
get the car fixed up myself,

299
00:14:13,039 --> 00:14:13,919
and chalk it up to bad luck.

300
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:17,559
Then the mechanic told me,

301
00:14:17,799 --> 00:14:20,039
he said it counts as property damage,

302
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:22,480
and it's considered a hit-and-run.

303
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:24,159
So I thought about it,

304
00:14:24,159 --> 00:14:24,840
this... this...

305
00:14:24,919 --> 00:14:25,879
wouldn't I be screwed?

306
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,399
So I rushed right over.

307
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,919
The traffic officers told me

308
00:14:31,399 --> 00:14:33,159
that Chen Qingchun took the blame

309
00:14:33,639 --> 00:14:34,559
and already paid the fine.

310
00:14:35,799 --> 00:14:36,759
I figured

311
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:38,240
that would be the end of it.

312
00:14:38,519 --> 00:14:40,200
Didn't expect to hear the broadcast today,

313
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:41,519
only to realize it isn't over.

314
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:43,399
Why would Chen Qingchun falsely confess?

315
00:14:43,759 --> 00:14:44,559
Didn't you ask him?

316
00:14:48,519 --> 00:14:49,639
It wasn't easy

317
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,279
getting everyone together,

318
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:55,120
and Qian Yichuan went and ruined it all.

319
00:15:01,399 --> 00:15:02,080
Chief Engineer Chen,

320
00:15:03,159 --> 00:15:03,919
there's one more thing.

321
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,000
What's this?

322
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:12,840
For me?

323
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:14,639
A leg of lamb.

324
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:16,080
Take it.

325
00:15:17,519 --> 00:15:18,320
What's this for?

326
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,519
You did me a huge favor.

327
00:15:21,519 --> 00:15:22,559
You really came through for me.

328
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:23,720
I...

329
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:27,919
About hitting that sculpture.

330
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:29,960
The one by the factory gate.

331
00:15:36,039 --> 00:15:36,759
Look,

332
00:15:37,519 --> 00:15:38,279
my lips are sealed.

333
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:39,919
I didn't tell a soul.

334
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:40,759
No, wait.

335
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,120
Why did you go

336
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:46,120
to the traffic police and take the fall for me?

337
00:15:46,679 --> 00:15:47,639
If it wasn't sorted out cleanly,

338
00:15:47,639 --> 00:15:49,000
I wouldn't have peace of mind.

339
00:15:51,639 --> 00:15:54,200
I went to Chen Yuan's place that day.

340
00:15:54,919 --> 00:15:56,840
The two of us had a few drinks.

341
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:59,320
Then I got a bit sleepy.

342
00:16:00,519 --> 00:16:01,840
He told me not to go back,

343
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,039
just sleep over at his place.

344
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:04,879
But then,

345
00:16:04,919 --> 00:16:06,240
I woke up in the middle of the night.

346
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:08,799
And I just wanted to go home.

347
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:12,320
At the time, I felt like I was pretty...

348
00:16:12,559 --> 00:16:13,639
pretty sober.

349
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:17,240
I figured there'd be no one on the road so late.

350
00:16:17,679 --> 00:16:20,320
Besides, it had been a long time since I drank.

351
00:16:20,879 --> 00:16:22,240
So I drove back.

352
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,960
When I passed by the brewery,

353
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:28,000
a big truck came from the other way.

354
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:30,320
That bastard had his high beams on,

355
00:16:30,399 --> 00:16:32,120
blinding me so I couldn't see a thing.

356
00:16:32,159 --> 00:16:33,279
In a moment of panic,

357
00:16:33,559 --> 00:16:35,039
I must have jerked the steering wheel.

358
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:35,840
*Bam!*

359
00:16:36,639 --> 00:16:37,600
Smashed right into that sculpture.

360
00:16:37,879 --> 00:16:38,840
Holy crap!

361
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:41,000
The exact same thing happened to us!

362
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,320
Me too!

363
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:43,639
Ran into a bastard

364
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:44,759
with high beams on.

365
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:45,679
Blinded me so bad...

366
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:46,159
I went *bam!*

367
00:16:47,519 --> 00:16:48,600
Hit twice in one night!

368
00:16:49,759 --> 00:16:51,759
You must have crashed right where I hit it!

369
00:16:51,799 --> 00:16:52,759
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

370
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:54,360
But I couldn't tell at all.

371
00:16:54,519 --> 00:16:56,039
Just slammed right into it!

372
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:57,360
You weren't hurt, right?

373
00:16:57,519 --> 00:16:57,879
I'm fine, I'm fine.

374
00:16:57,919 --> 00:16:58,600
Look at that.

375
00:16:59,799 --> 00:17:00,600
How much was the fine?

376
00:17:01,879 --> 00:17:02,240
Forget it.

377
00:17:02,919 --> 00:17:03,879
It's all in the past now.

378
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:04,680
Don't worry about it.

379
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:05,240
That won't do.

380
00:17:05,279 --> 00:17:06,279
I... I've already taken care of it.

381
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:06,880
No, no way.

382
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,119
Can't let you handle it alone.

383
00:17:08,839 --> 00:17:09,400
It's fine, really.

384
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:10,240
Take the leg of lamb.

385
00:17:10,839 --> 00:17:11,200
No, don't, don't.

386
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:11,519
Keep it.

387
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:12,240
I've got plenty.

388
00:17:12,599 --> 00:17:13,319
Come on, now.

389
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:15,119
You run a restaurant here,

390
00:17:16,119 --> 00:17:17,079
with lots of customers.

391
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:17,640
You keep it.

392
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:18,359
No, really, don't.

393
00:17:19,799 --> 00:17:20,359
Don't be polite.

394
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:21,119
No, I really can't.

395
00:17:29,559 --> 00:17:30,480
Bro, you can sit over there in a bit.

396
00:17:33,119 --> 00:17:33,759
With my legs,

397
00:17:33,799 --> 00:17:34,880
standing feels better.

398
00:17:43,359 --> 00:17:45,200
What right do you have to bring me here?

399
00:17:46,119 --> 00:17:47,839
Would we bring you here for no reason?

400
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,680
Xiao Wu, shut the door.

401
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,000
Take a seat.

402
00:17:52,839 --> 00:17:53,640
Cooperate with our investigation.

403
00:18:06,759 --> 00:18:07,400
Chief Engineer Chen,

404
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:08,960
you're quite something.

405
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:12,240
Traffic police inspected the scene.

406
00:18:12,319 --> 00:18:13,200
They said that sculpture

407
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:14,599
was hit by a minivan

408
00:18:14,599 --> 00:18:16,400
going over sixty kilometers an hour.

409
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:18,279
I remember you drive a Santana.

410
00:18:19,039 --> 00:18:19,720
It went flying.

411
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:22,319
And the repair shop said

412
00:18:22,319 --> 00:18:23,759
all you replaced was a bumper.

413
00:18:24,519 --> 00:18:25,680
Pretty solid car, huh?

414
00:18:26,319 --> 00:18:27,720
Over sixty kilometers an hour,

415
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:29,039
and just a bumper replaced.

416
00:18:31,599 --> 00:18:32,519
Cheng Youtian already confessed.

417
00:18:32,839 --> 00:18:33,400
He's the one who hit it.

418
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,640
Now you're the one lying to us.

419
00:18:37,279 --> 00:18:38,799
The real issue here is,

420
00:18:39,119 --> 00:18:41,440
the day the sculpture was hit and Cao Jun's death

421
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:42,480
happened at the exact same time.

422
00:18:43,359 --> 00:18:45,119
Why choose this exact moment

423
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,640
to take the fall?

424
00:18:47,279 --> 00:18:49,000
Taking the blame for a minor offense

425
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:49,680
to cover up a major crime,

426
00:18:49,759 --> 00:18:50,200
aren't you?

427
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:52,559
Setting yourself up with an alibi.

428
00:18:53,079 --> 00:18:54,079
Pretty calculating of you.

429
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:02,200
Know what this is?

430
00:19:02,519 --> 00:19:03,440
Didn't you know

431
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:04,880
Cao Jun kept a diary?

432
00:19:06,599 --> 00:19:08,599
He wrote in this diary

433
00:19:08,599 --> 00:19:10,680
that he found the traitor who betrayed the workers.

434
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,480
That traitor is you, isn't it?

435
00:19:14,599 --> 00:19:15,359
Let me tell you something.

436
00:19:16,319 --> 00:19:17,359
We've moved to a different room,

437
00:19:17,559 --> 00:19:18,759
and things have taken a serious turn.

438
00:19:19,319 --> 00:19:20,759
You can keep glaring at me

439
00:19:20,799 --> 00:19:21,759
and making a scene like before.

440
00:19:21,839 --> 00:19:23,039
But I hope you realize

441
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,519
I'm giving you a chance here.

442
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:27,440
Think it through

443
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:29,160
before you open your mouth.

444
00:19:37,599 --> 00:19:38,839
I'm the traitor.

445
00:19:47,319 --> 00:19:48,119
I was the one...

446
00:19:50,359 --> 00:19:51,279
who killed Cao Jun.

447
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:58,160
It all started back in '99 when the plant was sold.

448
00:20:09,680 --> 00:20:10,279
What is it?

449
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:11,960
Hesitating now?

450
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:14,839
Did you forget you joined their bunch

451
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:16,960
only after we talked it over?

452
00:20:17,519 --> 00:20:19,200
What now, did they turn you?

453
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:20,519
Getting cold feet?

454
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:21,599
No.

455
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:22,720
Lately...

456
00:20:22,759 --> 00:20:23,519
everyone

457
00:20:24,319 --> 00:20:25,720
is worried about being laid off,

458
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:28,200
scared of losing their livelihoods.

459
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:30,640
Old Chen,

460
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:31,599
there are no outsiders here.

461
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:32,920
Stop beating around the bush.

462
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Hurry up and let me see it.

463
00:20:34,119 --> 00:20:35,000
Let's see what they're scheming.

464
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:36,720
Well...

465
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:39,599
If we win the bid this time

466
00:20:39,599 --> 00:20:40,359
and I become director,

467
00:20:40,519 --> 00:20:41,279
I'm number one,

468
00:20:41,319 --> 00:20:42,480
and you're number two.

469
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:43,279
Aside from me,

470
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:44,720
you'll be the top boss in our plant.

471
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:45,480
You get it?

472
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:47,359
Well, over on their side,

473
00:20:47,759 --> 00:20:49,359
I'm at least number two as well.

474
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:50,720
Besides,

475
00:20:51,519 --> 00:20:52,519
I'm a major shareholder.

476
00:20:55,319 --> 00:20:56,920
Did you

477
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:58,000
put up any cash over there?

478
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:01,839
You always have to invest some cash, right?

479
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:06,039
Tell you what.

480
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:07,359
When I become director,

481
00:21:08,279 --> 00:21:10,119
you won't pay a single cent with me,

482
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:12,599
and I'll double the shares they gave you.

483
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:13,799
Deal?

484
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:15,920
What's more,

485
00:21:16,559 --> 00:21:17,559
once I'm director,

486
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:19,079
I'll send people...

487
00:21:19,599 --> 00:21:21,160
send you abroad

488
00:21:21,319 --> 00:21:22,079
on an inspection tour.

489
00:21:22,319 --> 00:21:23,400
We'll bring in some new machinery

490
00:21:23,519 --> 00:21:24,839
and boost our production.

491
00:21:25,279 --> 00:21:26,359
Everything on the tech side,

492
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,079
you'll have the final say.

493
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:27,880
You'll call the shots.

494
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:28,680
Sound good?

495
00:21:29,759 --> 00:21:30,279
Really?

496
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:31,480
Absolutely.

497
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:32,640
When I, Ma Guowen, give my word,

498
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,319
a promise is a promise,

499
00:21:34,319 --> 00:21:34,880
and it's carved in stone.

500
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:40,880
Director Ma,

501
00:21:41,559 --> 00:21:43,119
you're basically setting me up

502
00:21:43,799 --> 00:21:44,960
to look heartless and disloyal, huh?

503
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:45,519
Well...

504
00:21:45,640 --> 00:21:45,960
You...

505
00:21:46,759 --> 00:21:47,519
You know,

506
00:21:47,759 --> 00:21:48,759
the way you educated folks talk,

507
00:21:48,799 --> 00:21:50,240
it really gets on my nerves.

508
00:21:51,359 --> 00:21:52,480
Auction organizer,

509
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:53,480
bidders,

510
00:21:53,559 --> 00:21:55,119
reserve price setting...

511
00:21:55,599 --> 00:21:57,240
This is put together in real detail.

512
00:21:57,279 --> 00:21:58,240
Pretty comprehensive, too.

513
00:21:58,759 --> 00:22:00,079
You came well prepared, huh?

514
00:22:04,519 --> 00:22:05,000
Old Chen.

515
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,599
The man I know...

516
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,079
can not only help you,

517
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,359
but can help your son too.

518
00:22:09,920 --> 00:22:10,640
Who?

519
00:22:12,480 --> 00:22:13,559
I'll take you to meet him in a bit.

520
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:14,319
No, don't wait.

521
00:22:14,359 --> 00:22:15,039
Let's go right now.

522
00:22:15,119 --> 00:22:15,559
Let's go.

523
00:22:16,039 --> 00:22:17,000
That guy has serious clout.

524
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,119
Are you serious?

525
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:23,559
Guowen, please, come on in.

526
00:22:23,559 --> 00:22:23,920
Old Chen.

527
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:24,359
Come in, come in.

528
00:22:24,359 --> 00:22:24,880
Please, come in.

529
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:25,400
Come on in.

530
00:22:27,079 --> 00:22:27,680
I say, Guowen...

531
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:28,359
look at you.

532
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:29,759
Why did you bring gifts?

533
00:22:29,839 --> 00:22:30,680
It's the least I could do.

534
00:22:31,039 --> 00:22:31,839
Let me introduce you.

535
00:22:31,839 --> 00:22:33,440
Our brewery's Chief Engineer, Chen Qingchun.

536
00:22:34,079 --> 00:22:35,039
And I don't need to introduce this man, right?

537
00:22:35,079 --> 00:22:36,319
In the prime of his life at the ICB,

538
00:22:36,319 --> 00:22:38,279
the renowned Director of the ICB, Zheng Aimin.

539
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:39,319
Director Zheng.

540
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:40,240
Hello, hello.

541
00:22:40,279 --> 00:22:41,079
Hello, hello, hello.

542
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:41,599
Hello.

543
00:22:41,759 --> 00:22:42,240
Chief Chen.

544
00:22:42,440 --> 00:22:42,839
Good, good, good.

545
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:43,240
Come, come.

546
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:43,559
Sit down, please sit.

547
00:22:43,599 --> 00:22:44,160
Make yourselves at home.

548
00:22:48,039 --> 00:22:48,400
Old Chen.

549
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:49,839
Director Zheng's home...

550
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:51,400
not just anyone can come here.

551
00:22:52,039 --> 00:22:52,359
Yes, indeed.

552
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:53,319
Work hard with me,

553
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:54,680
and you won't be shortchanged.

554
00:22:59,039 --> 00:23:00,079
It's pretty warm inside.

555
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:01,480
Here, Guowen.

556
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:02,680
Here, Chief Chen.

557
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:03,680
Thank you, thank you.

558
00:23:07,039 --> 00:23:08,079
What is this?

559
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,200
It's so soft.

560
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:09,920
So comfortable.

561
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:12,039
It's from Siberia.

562
00:23:13,519 --> 00:23:14,400
If you like it,

563
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:15,960
I'll have him get a couple for you later.

564
00:23:16,799 --> 00:23:18,279
Well... I couldn't possibly.

565
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,440
Director Zheng's place has tons of nice things.

566
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:21,440
Say, Director Zheng,

567
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,559
regarding this auction,

568
00:23:23,640 --> 00:23:24,680
Qingchun really pulled his weight.

569
00:23:25,480 --> 00:23:27,400
He's definitely our top guy at the brewery.

570
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:28,680
Impressive.

571
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:29,559
You flatter me.

572
00:23:29,559 --> 00:23:30,119
He's capable.

573
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:31,319
I wouldn't have brought him here otherwise.

574
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:32,160
That's true.

575
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,119
Tell you what,

576
00:23:34,319 --> 00:23:35,519
nobody leaves today.

577
00:23:36,119 --> 00:23:38,400
Let's have a few drinks at my place.

578
00:23:38,839 --> 00:23:39,519
Oh, man!

579
00:23:41,079 --> 00:23:42,279
Director Zheng, you're too kind!

580
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:42,960
Oh, man!

581
00:23:43,039 --> 00:23:44,079
Once we're here, we won't leave!

582
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,119
How many times do I have to say it?

583
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:49,000
There's a thief inside the factory!

584
00:23:49,039 --> 00:23:49,480
You people are fine.

585
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:50,640
The biggest thief is Ma Guowen!

586
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:51,519
Go back right now!

587
00:23:51,559 --> 00:23:53,559
Ma Guowen embezzled two million from the brewery!

588
00:23:54,119 --> 00:23:55,000
You're in the security section.

589
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:56,119
You should know the law.

590
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:58,279
Which law says we can't buy the factory?

591
00:23:58,319 --> 00:23:58,680
That's right!

592
00:23:58,720 --> 00:23:59,200
On what grounds?

593
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:00,000
Let me tell you, that's right!

594
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:02,519
Everything Ma Guowen embezzled is state property!

595
00:24:02,799 --> 00:24:03,960
And our benefits!

596
00:24:04,319 --> 00:24:05,240
Stop talking nonsense!

597
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:06,799
Are you letting me out or not?

598
00:24:06,839 --> 00:24:07,519
Who do you think you are?

599
00:24:07,559 --> 00:24:08,759
Tomorrow this factory is ours!

600
00:24:08,799 --> 00:24:09,480
Who do you think you are?

601
00:24:09,480 --> 00:24:09,920
If you don't let us out,

602
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:10,680
you're fired tomorrow!

603
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:11,440
You're not getting out!

604
00:24:17,519 --> 00:24:19,039
We're all from the same plant,

605
00:24:19,480 --> 00:24:20,039
right?

606
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:30,160
Director Cheng!

607
00:24:30,839 --> 00:24:31,480
Director Cheng!

608
00:24:31,839 --> 00:24:32,240
Hurry!

609
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:33,079
Hurry, come quick!

610
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:34,079
Hurry!

611
00:24:37,599 --> 00:24:39,039
I got in touch with Xuemei.

612
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:40,319
She already took a cab

613
00:24:40,559 --> 00:24:42,720
from Qingzhou to the auction site.

614
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:43,759
That's great.

615
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:45,200
Leaving this to Xuemei

616
00:24:45,519 --> 00:24:46,039
is the right call.

617
00:24:46,119 --> 00:24:46,680
Yeah.

618
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:47,839
Then that's that.

619
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:49,039
Stop arguing with them.

620
00:24:49,039 --> 00:24:49,559
Let's pull back.

621
00:24:49,599 --> 00:24:50,960
Right. Okay, tell everyone to head back.

622
00:24:51,119 --> 00:24:51,519
Head back, head back.

623
00:24:51,519 --> 00:24:52,000
All right.

624
00:24:58,640 --> 00:24:59,240
Everyone from the workshop,

625
00:24:59,359 --> 00:25:00,160
head back now! Head back!

626
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:00,680
Head back, that's right.

627
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:01,839
Stop arguing with them!

628
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:02,279
Right.

629
00:25:04,839 --> 00:25:05,200
Let's go.

630
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:06,440
Clear out, clear out, clear out!

631
00:25:07,119 --> 00:25:07,599
Make it quick!

632
00:25:11,039 --> 00:25:12,559
Give me the director's office key.

633
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:13,319
What do you need the key for?

634
00:25:13,319 --> 00:25:13,960
Back to the workshop!

635
00:25:14,319 --> 00:25:15,000
Everyone back! Give it to me.

636
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:16,240
Here, here, here.

637
00:25:16,319 --> 00:25:16,880
This is...

638
00:25:17,359 --> 00:25:17,759
Go!

639
00:25:17,799 --> 00:25:18,319
I know.

640
00:25:18,440 --> 00:25:18,839
Go!

641
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:19,480
Let's go!

642
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:48,000
Hello, Director Ma.

643
00:25:48,759 --> 00:25:50,000
There's a change of plans.

644
00:25:51,319 --> 00:25:54,039
Cheng Youtian had Liu Xuemei represent everyone

645
00:25:54,279 --> 00:25:56,160
and attend the auction.

646
00:25:57,039 --> 00:25:59,079
She took a cab over from Qingzhou.

647
00:25:59,799 --> 00:26:00,799
Listen up, everyone.

648
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:02,880
Our lovely Chief Engineer Chen

649
00:26:03,079 --> 00:26:04,720
called me in a total panic.

650
00:26:05,039 --> 00:26:05,519
"Holy crap!

651
00:26:05,559 --> 00:26:06,279
Things went south!

652
00:26:06,559 --> 00:26:07,680
They changed their plan!

653
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:10,519
They brought Liu Xuemei in from Qingzhou!

654
00:26:10,519 --> 00:26:12,359
Told me to get her under control right away!"

655
00:26:12,359 --> 00:26:12,920
Man, oh man.

656
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:13,759
He was scared half to death.

657
00:26:13,759 --> 00:26:14,720
You should've seen how nervous he was.

658
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:17,720
I said, "Old Chen,

659
00:26:18,079 --> 00:26:20,319
that whole room is full of my people.

660
00:26:21,079 --> 00:26:22,519
Doesn't matter who comes, it won't do any good."

661
00:26:22,799 --> 00:26:23,480
Am I right?

662
00:26:26,279 --> 00:26:26,880
Old Chen,

663
00:26:27,200 --> 00:26:28,599
this turned out great.

664
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:31,000
Everyone thinks Liu Xuemei is a traitor now.

665
00:26:31,039 --> 00:26:32,000
Nobody's talking about you anymore.

666
00:26:32,279 --> 00:26:33,119
You're off the hook.

667
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:33,960
Just relax.

668
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:35,960
When Liu Xuemei was drinking with me,

669
00:26:36,559 --> 00:26:38,279
I slapped that cash down in front of her.

670
00:26:38,319 --> 00:26:39,480
Her eyes lit right up.

671
00:26:39,519 --> 00:26:40,759
She sat right down on my lap

672
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:42,039
and wouldn't budge even if I pushed.

673
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:44,039
Kept toasting me drink after drink.

674
00:26:44,759 --> 00:26:45,519
People...

675
00:26:45,559 --> 00:26:46,480
Once they see money,

676
00:26:48,359 --> 00:26:49,359
they change just like that.

677
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:53,519
Don't you worry.

678
00:26:57,559 --> 00:26:58,039
Director.

679
00:26:58,599 --> 00:26:59,279
Director Zheng has arrived.

680
00:27:00,599 --> 00:27:01,000
Come on, come on.

681
00:27:01,039 --> 00:27:01,640
Let's welcome him.

682
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:02,000
Come on.

683
00:27:04,839 --> 00:27:05,680
Sorry about that.

684
00:27:05,759 --> 00:27:06,240
I'm late.

685
00:27:06,319 --> 00:27:06,920
Not at all, not at all.

686
00:27:06,920 --> 00:27:07,359
Had a meeting just now.

687
00:27:07,640 --> 00:27:08,400
You're right on time.

688
00:27:08,519 --> 00:27:08,880
Quick, quick.

689
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:09,640
Come in, please.

690
00:27:09,640 --> 00:27:10,119
We've been waiting for you.

691
00:27:10,119 --> 00:27:10,519
Have a seat.

692
00:27:10,640 --> 00:27:11,160
Guowen.

693
00:27:11,200 --> 00:27:12,880
You put on quite a show here.

694
00:27:13,119 --> 00:27:13,519
Only the best for you!

695
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:14,160
Director Zheng.

696
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:14,759
Good to see you.

697
00:27:14,799 --> 00:27:15,440
Engineer Chen is here too.

698
00:27:15,839 --> 00:27:16,319
Please, have a seat.

699
00:27:16,359 --> 00:27:16,680
Director Zheng.

700
00:27:16,720 --> 00:27:17,039
Come on, come on.

701
00:27:17,039 --> 00:27:17,640
Please, take a seat.

702
00:27:17,680 --> 00:27:18,440
We've got to make it lively.

703
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:18,960
Time to celebrate!

704
00:27:18,960 --> 00:27:19,599
Right?

705
00:27:20,079 --> 00:27:20,839
You take the head seat.

706
00:27:20,880 --> 00:27:21,359
Please, head of the table.

707
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:23,440
Come, sit down, sit down.

708
00:27:23,559 --> 00:27:24,119
Come on, everyone.

709
00:27:24,119 --> 00:27:24,759
Let's hear some applause!

710
00:27:28,039 --> 00:27:29,039
Put your hands together!

711
00:27:30,039 --> 00:27:30,759
As for me...

712
00:27:31,079 --> 00:27:32,200
I don't care for all this fuss.

713
00:27:33,240 --> 00:27:34,079
Besides...

714
00:27:34,279 --> 00:27:35,839
I'm not the star of the show today.

715
00:27:36,319 --> 00:27:38,279
It's our Director Ma Guowen.

716
00:27:39,799 --> 00:27:40,839
Lacheng Brewery...

717
00:27:40,960 --> 00:27:42,519
...will probably carry your name from now on.

718
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:45,119
I wouldn't dare, not at all.

719
00:27:45,519 --> 00:27:46,519
It won't just bear the name Ma.

720
00:27:46,599 --> 00:27:47,759
It'll carry the name Zheng too!

721
00:27:47,799 --> 00:27:48,400
Don't you think?

722
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:49,960
Now, Director Zheng,

723
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:50,440
please sit, sit down.

724
00:27:50,480 --> 00:27:51,039
Let's all sit.

725
00:27:51,119 --> 00:27:51,599
Sit down, sit down.

726
00:27:51,680 --> 00:27:53,640
Director Zheng came despite his busy schedule.

727
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:55,599
Well, since everyone's here,

728
00:27:57,640 --> 00:27:58,759
let me propose a toast.

729
00:27:59,839 --> 00:28:00,680
Everyone sitting at this table...

730
00:28:00,759 --> 00:28:02,000
...is one of our own.

731
00:28:02,200 --> 00:28:02,799
Moving forward,

732
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:03,799
this Lacheng Brewery of ours...

733
00:28:04,039 --> 00:28:05,079
...will rely entirely on all of you.

734
00:28:05,319 --> 00:28:06,759
Let's raise a glass to Director Zheng.

735
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:08,079
To Director Zheng!

736
00:28:08,359 --> 00:28:09,200
To Director Zheng!

737
00:28:09,359 --> 00:28:10,000
To Director Zheng!

738
00:28:10,319 --> 00:28:10,759
Drink up, everyone.

739
00:28:10,759 --> 00:28:11,079
Director Zheng.

740
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:15,039
You see...

741
00:28:15,640 --> 00:28:16,440
...when toasting...

742
00:28:16,480 --> 00:28:17,519
If your butt leaves the seat,

743
00:28:17,759 --> 00:28:18,640
the drink doesn't count!

744
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:20,480
So we...

745
00:28:20,519 --> 00:28:21,039
...should have another round!

746
00:28:21,039 --> 00:28:22,079
Another toast to Director Zheng!

747
00:28:22,079 --> 00:28:22,480
All right!

748
00:28:22,480 --> 00:28:23,000
Come on, bottoms up!

749
00:28:29,640 --> 00:28:31,200
Here's to everyone's good health!

750
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:32,039
Hear, hear!

751
00:28:32,079 --> 00:28:32,920
Hear, hear!

752
00:28:35,279 --> 00:28:36,960
I'm going to the restroom.

753
00:28:38,039 --> 00:28:38,799
Old Chen here...

754
00:28:38,839 --> 00:28:39,759
...is our plant's true hero.

755
00:28:40,599 --> 00:28:42,200
Actually, everyone sitting here today...

756
00:28:42,960 --> 00:28:44,200
...is a hero of our plant.

757
00:28:44,599 --> 00:28:47,039
This annual get-together for our veteran cadres...

758
00:28:47,039 --> 00:28:48,200
...and distinguished veterans...

759
00:28:48,319 --> 00:28:49,119
...we've got to keep it going.

760
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:50,160
We should meet up more often.

761
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:50,720
Right?

762
00:28:50,759 --> 00:28:52,279
Come on, bottoms up!

763
00:28:52,359 --> 00:28:52,640
Cheers!

764
00:28:52,680 --> 00:28:53,319
Come on, drink up!

765
00:28:56,119 --> 00:28:56,839
Cao Jun?

766
00:28:57,359 --> 00:28:58,119
What are you doing here?

767
00:28:58,720 --> 00:28:59,319
Old Chen.

768
00:29:01,079 --> 00:29:02,440
You just came out of that room, right?

769
00:29:03,359 --> 00:29:03,799
Yeah.

770
00:29:06,039 --> 00:29:06,440
Wait.

771
00:29:06,559 --> 00:29:07,039
Old Cao!

772
00:29:07,559 --> 00:29:08,119
Where are you going?

773
00:29:09,640 --> 00:29:10,359
I'm looking for Ma Guowen.

774
00:29:11,039 --> 00:29:11,519
Don't, don't, don't.

775
00:29:11,519 --> 00:29:12,160
Just go home.

776
00:29:12,519 --> 00:29:13,599
Listen to me. Don't do this.

777
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:14,839
You've been drinking, haven't you?

778
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:15,359
You've had too much.

779
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:16,240
Hurry up and head home.

780
00:29:16,440 --> 00:29:17,720
Go, go on.

781
00:29:19,839 --> 00:29:20,400
Cao Jun!

782
00:29:21,440 --> 00:29:22,400
Old Cao! Old Cao!

783
00:29:29,200 --> 00:29:29,920
Everyone's here, huh?

784
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:33,400
Drinking the good stuff, too.

785
00:29:35,599 --> 00:29:36,559
Eating well, aren't you?

786
00:29:37,279 --> 00:29:38,599
All big shots here, huh?

787
00:29:39,480 --> 00:29:40,519
Here I am with nothing to eat or drink,

788
00:29:40,519 --> 00:29:41,559
while you're all living it up.

789
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:43,319
Old Cao.

790
00:29:43,599 --> 00:29:44,359
What're you doing here?

791
00:29:44,519 --> 00:29:45,559
Came to see you.

792
00:29:45,759 --> 00:29:47,119
What did you bring that thing for?

793
00:29:47,599 --> 00:29:47,920
Take it.

794
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,240
Didn't you give me this?

795
00:29:49,319 --> 00:29:49,920
Afraid you'd forgotten,

796
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:50,759
so I brought it to show you.

797
00:29:51,920 --> 00:29:52,839
"Model Worker."

798
00:29:53,720 --> 00:29:54,599
Awarded to me by Director Ma.

799
00:29:54,640 --> 00:29:55,400
That's enough.

800
00:29:55,480 --> 00:29:56,440
Old Cao, just go home.

801
00:29:56,480 --> 00:29:57,200
Stop making a scene.

802
00:29:58,559 --> 00:29:59,839
It wasn't easy catching up with you.

803
00:30:00,160 --> 00:30:01,000
Why would I go back?

804
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:04,279
Anyway, I'm late.

805
00:30:04,680 --> 00:30:07,240
Let me drink a penalty glass first.

806
00:30:09,079 --> 00:30:09,960
A toast to everyone!

807
00:30:13,440 --> 00:30:14,200
That liquor's damn expensive!

808
00:30:14,200 --> 00:30:15,119
Go easy on it.

809
00:30:15,400 --> 00:30:16,039
Expensive, is it?

810
00:30:17,640 --> 00:30:18,440
Then I'd better drink more.

811
00:30:19,039 --> 00:30:19,640
All right, all right.

812
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:20,559
Don't drink so much.

813
00:30:24,440 --> 00:30:25,519
Don't be mad.

814
00:30:25,519 --> 00:30:26,119
What's there to be mad about?

815
00:30:26,240 --> 00:30:26,920
Just go home.

816
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:27,839
Stop embarrassing me here.

817
00:30:27,839 --> 00:30:28,319
No, listen...

818
00:30:28,599 --> 00:30:31,279
Lacheng Brewery is such a huge plant.

819
00:30:31,559 --> 00:30:32,799
Who... who else could be director?

820
00:30:33,359 --> 00:30:34,599
Only Director Ma has what it takes.

821
00:30:35,319 --> 00:30:35,799
Why?

822
00:30:36,319 --> 00:30:38,160
Because Ma Guowen can do it!

823
00:30:38,359 --> 00:30:39,359
He's no ordinary man.

824
00:30:39,640 --> 00:30:40,240
Right?

825
00:30:41,039 --> 00:30:42,559
Stop making a fool of yourself here, will you?

826
00:30:42,599 --> 00:30:43,559
Fine, fine, fine.

827
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:45,039
Old Ma...

828
00:30:45,079 --> 00:30:46,079
I've got things to take care of at home.

829
00:30:46,160 --> 00:30:46,799
I'll head out first.

830
00:30:46,839 --> 00:30:47,799
Wait, wait, Director Zheng!

831
00:30:48,799 --> 00:30:49,720
You're Director Zheng, right?

832
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:52,680
You... you don't recognize me, do you?

833
00:30:53,200 --> 00:30:54,039
Sure I do.

834
00:30:54,359 --> 00:30:55,240
Old Tao, right?

835
00:30:56,160 --> 00:30:57,039
Old Cao.

836
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:59,079
That guy's Old Tao.

837
00:31:00,119 --> 00:31:00,880
Cao Jun.

838
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:02,160
The forklift driver.

839
00:31:04,480 --> 00:31:04,839
Come on, come on.

840
00:31:04,839 --> 00:31:05,359
Sit, sit down.

841
00:31:05,400 --> 00:31:05,640
No.

842
00:31:05,640 --> 00:31:06,440
You sit. Sit, take a seat.

843
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:07,480
Excuse me, make way.

844
00:31:07,920 --> 00:31:08,519
Step aside.

845
00:31:08,559 --> 00:31:09,240
Let me speak to Director Zheng.

846
00:31:09,240 --> 00:31:09,799
Come on, really...

847
00:31:10,559 --> 00:31:11,119
Director Zheng.

848
00:31:11,720 --> 00:31:13,079
How did he follow you in?

849
00:31:13,240 --> 00:31:14,240
I have no idea.

850
00:31:14,480 --> 00:31:15,319
He just slipped right in behind me.

851
00:31:15,359 --> 00:31:15,799
As for me...

852
00:31:15,920 --> 00:31:16,599
How does he know I'm here?

853
00:31:16,599 --> 00:31:18,359
I'm a veteran of Lacheng Brewery.

854
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:21,200
I left Lacheng Brewery over ten years ago.

855
00:31:21,519 --> 00:31:23,640
Things have changed so much in these years.

856
00:31:23,960 --> 00:31:26,039
Some made it big, like Old Ma here,

857
00:31:26,599 --> 00:31:28,440
and some hit rock bottom like me.

858
00:31:29,039 --> 00:31:29,960
Sometimes I even...

859
00:31:30,039 --> 00:31:31,000
Sometimes I ask myself,

860
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:31,359
I say,

861
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:33,000
"What did you do?"

862
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:34,519
"How did your life end up like this?"

863
00:31:34,559 --> 00:31:35,000
Right?

864
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:35,400
Yeah.

865
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:38,319
Director Zheng,

866
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:40,799
you see,

867
00:31:41,920 --> 00:31:43,559
I joined Lacheng Brewery at 17.

868
00:31:44,200 --> 00:31:44,960
And my parents,

869
00:31:45,240 --> 00:31:46,000
they were both brewery lifers.

870
00:31:46,559 --> 00:31:47,559
I'm brewery stock,

871
00:31:47,759 --> 00:31:48,319
a true-blue brewery kid.

872
00:31:48,920 --> 00:31:50,200
Right, right, okay.

873
00:31:50,519 --> 00:31:51,759
Through job succession,

874
00:31:51,759 --> 00:31:52,759
I could've gone into brewing.

875
00:31:53,559 --> 00:31:54,400
I didn't care for brewing.

876
00:31:54,400 --> 00:31:55,559
I just loved driving a forklift.

877
00:31:55,799 --> 00:31:56,559
So I drove a forklift.

878
00:31:56,720 --> 00:31:57,200
That's good.

879
00:31:57,200 --> 00:31:58,640
Sure, driving a forklift,

880
00:31:58,720 --> 00:31:59,960
it wasn't as prestigious as brewing.

881
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:01,519
But if you do it well,

882
00:32:01,559 --> 00:32:02,640
I could still win Model Worker.

883
00:32:02,960 --> 00:32:04,400
Look at my Model Worker award.

884
00:32:04,759 --> 00:32:05,240
See?

885
00:32:05,480 --> 00:32:06,039
Here,

886
00:32:06,039 --> 00:32:06,680
this... right here.

887
00:32:07,079 --> 00:32:07,920
Old Ma presented it to me.

888
00:32:08,400 --> 00:32:08,839
This one,

889
00:32:09,119 --> 00:32:10,000
the Model Worker Representative.

890
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:10,480
This... this is my... that...

891
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:11,480
I should get going.

892
00:32:11,720 --> 00:32:12,200
Wait, wait!

893
00:32:12,279 --> 00:32:12,720
Don't leave!

894
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:13,319
Hey, what are you doing...

895
00:32:13,319 --> 00:32:14,160
You can't leave.

896
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:15,160
No, you can't leave.

897
00:32:15,720 --> 00:32:16,000
Look,

898
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:16,400
Director Zheng,

899
00:32:16,640 --> 00:32:17,759
it wasn't easy tracking you down.

900
00:32:17,799 --> 00:32:18,880
Hear me out! A high-ranking director like you—

901
00:32:19,079 --> 00:32:19,559
Hear what out?!

902
00:32:19,559 --> 00:32:20,119
Just hear me out!

903
00:32:20,119 --> 00:32:20,680
Hear what out?!

904
00:32:21,119 --> 00:32:22,720
Director Zheng retired long ago!

905
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:24,720
Talking to him won't do any good!

906
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:27,200
Retired?

907
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:28,359
Retired!

908
00:32:28,960 --> 00:32:29,599
Really retired?

909
00:32:29,640 --> 00:32:30,319
Really!

910
00:32:30,759 --> 00:32:31,759
Then what the hell am I chatting with you for?

911
00:32:31,759 --> 00:32:32,720
Wasting my breath on you...

912
00:32:32,759 --> 00:32:33,279
Should've said so earlier!

913
00:32:33,319 --> 00:32:33,799
He's retired.

914
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:37,319
Old Ma,

915
00:32:38,240 --> 00:32:39,359
can we have a heart-to-heart?

916
00:32:41,119 --> 00:32:41,720
Look,

917
00:32:42,119 --> 00:32:42,799
deep down,

918
00:32:44,240 --> 00:32:46,119
what kind of person am I, Cao Jun?

919
00:32:46,519 --> 00:32:47,839
You're a great guy.

920
00:32:48,359 --> 00:32:50,359
You're a model worker.

921
00:32:50,480 --> 00:32:51,960
Otherwise, why give you that banner?

922
00:32:52,079 --> 00:32:52,920
Why else would we?

923
00:32:53,559 --> 00:32:54,400
Just go home,

924
00:32:55,519 --> 00:32:56,200
all right?

925
00:32:57,440 --> 00:32:58,880
Bullshit!

926
00:33:00,960 --> 00:33:01,720
In your eyes,

927
00:33:02,000 --> 00:33:04,079
I'm just a pushover.

928
00:33:05,480 --> 00:33:07,279
A pushover anyone can walk all over!

929
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:09,839
Ma Guowen, tell the truth!

930
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:11,720
Don't you think I'm just one of those...

931
00:33:11,759 --> 00:33:12,119
those...

932
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:15,480
who take every beating and insult without a peep,

933
00:33:15,559 --> 00:33:16,559
one of that kind?

934
00:33:17,599 --> 00:33:18,359
I never said that.

935
00:33:19,039 --> 00:33:19,839
You didn't say it!

936
00:33:21,799 --> 00:33:22,680
It's my fault too.

937
00:33:24,119 --> 00:33:26,279
I don't usually talk much,

938
00:33:26,880 --> 00:33:27,880
You've talked plenty today.

939
00:33:27,960 --> 00:33:29,039
and I don't have many friends.

940
00:33:30,680 --> 00:33:32,759
All day long, I just tinker with

941
00:33:33,119 --> 00:33:34,400
those useless little things.

942
00:33:34,480 --> 00:33:35,640
In your words,

943
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:37,200
I'm the kind of guy

944
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:41,000
who can neither govern nor fight.

945
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,160
But...

946
00:33:46,319 --> 00:33:48,319
even if I, Cao Jun, am completely useless,

947
00:33:48,440 --> 00:33:50,119
you, Ma Guowen, can't bully me like this!

948
00:33:50,720 --> 00:33:52,759
I used a forklift to haul your stuff,

949
00:33:52,759 --> 00:33:54,200
and I ended up having to pay you!

950
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:54,880
How is that fair?

951
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:56,160
Even if I have no brains,

952
00:33:56,160 --> 00:33:57,400
whether I broke that glass,

953
00:33:57,400 --> 00:33:58,079
wouldn't I know?

954
00:33:58,160 --> 00:33:58,839
You messed with me for so long

955
00:33:58,880 --> 00:33:59,960
just over the money for that glass?

956
00:33:59,960 --> 00:34:00,960
Just for the glass?

957
00:34:01,079 --> 00:34:02,640
When are you giving back my share capital?

958
00:34:03,359 --> 00:34:04,200
How many years did I pay into it?

959
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:04,880
Did you ever give it back?

960
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:06,200
The holiday grocery allowance,

961
00:34:06,240 --> 00:34:06,920
didn't we hand that out?

962
00:34:06,920 --> 00:34:08,199
Is that grocery pocket change enough,

963
00:34:08,239 --> 00:34:10,480
enough to match the bank interest on my shares?

964
00:34:10,840 --> 00:34:11,800
You're just bullying me!

965
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:12,559
Ma Guowen!

966
00:34:13,199 --> 00:34:13,880
Security!

967
00:34:13,960 --> 00:34:14,840
Even if Director Zheng stepped down,

968
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:15,719
you can still back me up! Waiter!

969
00:34:15,800 --> 00:34:16,639
And you all!

970
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:17,360
You guys!

971
00:34:17,440 --> 00:34:18,400
He insists that I...

972
00:34:18,400 --> 00:34:19,559
I... that the glass

973
00:34:19,639 --> 00:34:20,599
I hauled off was broken by me!

974
00:34:20,679 --> 00:34:21,280
I... I...

975
00:34:21,360 --> 00:34:22,480
Even if I'm a complete bastard,

976
00:34:22,559 --> 00:34:23,920
I didn't break your damn glass!

977
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:25,480
Why the hell do you say I broke it?

978
00:34:26,039 --> 00:34:27,639
Why do I have to live like this?

979
00:34:27,719 --> 00:34:29,400
When I was down on my luck, did any of you help me?

980
00:34:29,599 --> 00:34:30,119
Let me handle it, let me handle it.

981
00:34:30,119 --> 00:34:30,679
You're still acting like this.

982
00:34:31,840 --> 00:34:32,360
Don't touch me!

983
00:34:32,519 --> 00:34:32,920
No...

984
00:34:33,400 --> 00:34:35,360
Director Zheng, even if you retired, hear me out!

985
00:34:35,440 --> 00:34:37,039
Ma Guowen, you bastard!

986
00:34:37,119 --> 00:34:38,280
You bastard!

987
00:34:38,519 --> 00:34:39,159
Let go of me!

988
00:34:39,440 --> 00:34:40,840
Both of you, let go of me!

989
00:34:41,159 --> 00:34:42,079
Are you going to let go?

990
00:34:42,239 --> 00:34:42,639
If you don't let go,

991
00:34:42,679 --> 00:34:43,360
I'll smash my head in right here!

992
00:34:43,480 --> 00:34:44,400
Let go of me! All right, all right.

993
00:34:44,559 --> 00:34:45,119
Let him go.

994
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:46,719
Cao Jun,

995
00:34:47,119 --> 00:34:47,880
stop making a scene.

996
00:34:48,280 --> 00:34:49,000
Just go home.

997
00:34:59,800 --> 00:35:00,400
What do you want?

998
00:35:08,239 --> 00:35:09,239
Chen Qingchun,

999
00:35:11,280 --> 00:35:12,599
don't think I don't know

1000
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:16,679
what you did.

1001
00:35:39,280 --> 00:35:40,480
Ma Guowen's dead.

1002
00:35:40,800 --> 00:35:42,000
You're not getting off easy either.

1003
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:04,199
Hello?

1004
00:36:04,559 --> 00:36:05,800
The money's all ready.

1005
00:36:06,519 --> 00:36:07,159
Cash.

1006
00:36:07,960 --> 00:36:09,719
Under the Qianjin Road overpass,

1007
00:36:09,920 --> 00:36:10,880
100 meters north.

1008
00:36:11,840 --> 00:36:12,719
Two o'clock.

1009
00:36:14,639 --> 00:36:15,559
Don't be late.

1010
00:36:16,440 --> 00:36:16,920
Got it.

1011
00:36:57,239 --> 00:36:57,840
Where's my money?

1012
00:36:59,159 --> 00:36:59,760
In the trunk.

1013
00:37:00,280 --> 00:37:00,920
Get it yourself.

1014
00:39:31,480 --> 00:39:32,639
Another person died last night.

1015
00:39:32,719 --> 00:39:33,360
Where at?

1016
00:39:33,400 --> 00:39:34,039
On Qianjin Road.

1017
00:39:34,920 --> 00:39:36,760
They haven't even cracked the case from the other day.

1018
00:39:36,800 --> 00:39:38,239
Ma Guowen's case

1019
00:39:38,559 --> 00:39:39,320
still isn't solved.

1020
00:39:39,360 --> 00:39:39,960
Yeah.

1021
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:41,159
How did another one die?

1022
00:39:41,199 --> 00:39:41,920
Who is it this time?

1023
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:43,639
The forklift driver from the brewery.

1024
00:39:43,719 --> 00:39:44,320
Cao Jun.

1025
00:39:44,840 --> 00:39:45,880
Someone killed him.

1026
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:46,800
Cao Jun? Cao Jun?!

1027
00:39:46,880 --> 00:39:48,119
Cao Jun got killed?

1028
00:39:48,239 --> 00:39:48,840
Yeah. Holy crap.

1029
00:39:48,840 --> 00:39:50,119
That punk always loved showing off. Chief Engineer Chen,

1030
00:39:50,119 --> 00:39:51,119
did you hear? That kid...

1031
00:39:51,519 --> 00:39:52,159
Just heard.

1032
00:39:54,440 --> 00:39:55,239
Let me grab my hard hat first.

1033
00:39:58,559 --> 00:39:59,400
Last night...

1034
00:39:59,840 --> 00:40:00,440
Who would've thought? I mean,

1035
00:40:00,679 --> 00:40:02,239
he must've pissed someone off. Just the other day,

1036
00:40:02,239 --> 00:40:03,880
I saw Cao Jun on Qianjin Road.

1037
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:05,039
He must've crossed someone. How did he just...

1038
00:40:05,039 --> 00:40:05,760
end up dead?

1039
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:10,239
What time did the hit happen?

1040
00:40:10,639 --> 00:40:11,440
No idea.

1041
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:13,440
It was already like this first thing in the morning.

1042
00:40:13,679 --> 00:40:14,039
Then...

1043
00:40:14,119 --> 00:40:15,639
Didn't anyone on duty hear a thing?

1044
00:40:15,719 --> 00:40:17,599
Your plant is right on the main road.

1045
00:40:18,480 --> 00:40:19,599
There are no surveillance cameras here.

1046
00:40:19,599 --> 00:40:20,679
Where would you find cameras?

1047
00:40:20,719 --> 00:40:22,039
Look how old this place is.

1048
00:40:22,679 --> 00:40:23,440
Good grief.

1049
00:40:23,920 --> 00:40:24,679
Cao Jun is gone.

1050
00:40:24,880 --> 00:40:25,440
What the hell?

1051
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:26,039
Come here for a second.

1052
00:40:27,079 --> 00:40:28,760
Someone killed him under the bridge.

1053
00:40:28,840 --> 00:40:30,079
Why would someone kill Cao Jun?

1054
00:40:31,360 --> 00:40:33,199
Still no word on Director Ma, and now Cao Jun...

1055
00:40:33,400 --> 00:40:34,760
Did anyone see what vehicle it was?

1056
00:40:35,280 --> 00:40:37,599
Couldn't see, officer. It was pitch black.

1057
00:40:37,840 --> 00:40:39,440
Why're the cops looking for you? You a suspect?

1058
00:40:39,440 --> 00:40:40,239
How could I be a suspect?

1059
00:40:40,239 --> 00:40:40,960
Traffic cops.

1060
00:40:41,559 --> 00:40:42,760
I'm telling you, he got hit hard.

1061
00:40:42,760 --> 00:40:44,239
Quite a few people died these past few days.

1062
00:40:44,360 --> 00:40:45,480
It's creepy as hell, let me tell you.

1063
00:40:45,480 --> 00:40:46,119
Cao Jun is gone.

1064
00:40:46,559 --> 00:40:46,960
Gone.

1065
00:40:46,960 --> 00:40:47,440
Officer...

1066
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:49,239
I'm so sorry.

1067
00:40:49,840 --> 00:40:50,280
This...

1068
00:40:50,800 --> 00:40:51,440
I was the one who hit him.

1069
00:40:51,639 --> 00:40:52,280
Move along, move along.

1070
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:53,119
Go on, let's go.

1071
00:40:53,119 --> 00:40:53,880
You hit him?

1072
00:40:54,119 --> 00:40:55,280
It was pitch black.

1073
00:40:55,280 --> 00:40:56,000
I didn't see him.

1074
00:40:56,440 --> 00:40:57,920
I thought my truck just broke down.

1075
00:40:58,440 --> 00:40:59,159
Nothing seemed wrong,

1076
00:40:59,679 --> 00:41:00,760
but now I realize...

1077
00:41:00,960 --> 00:41:02,039
Then come with me to

1078
00:41:02,400 --> 00:41:02,920
the traffic division.

1079
00:41:04,000 --> 00:41:04,519
Okay.

1080
00:41:21,880 --> 00:41:22,400
Something's not right.

1081
00:41:23,039 --> 00:41:23,760
It still doesn't add up.

1082
00:41:24,440 --> 00:41:24,960
What's wrong?

1083
00:41:25,360 --> 00:41:26,719
I think there's more to this.

1084
00:41:28,599 --> 00:41:29,599
He killed Cao Jun

1085
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:30,480
and confessed.

1086
00:41:31,239 --> 00:41:32,199
What's off about that?

1087
00:41:32,559 --> 00:41:34,079
Sure, he confessed,

1088
00:41:34,679 --> 00:41:37,239
but I think the motive is too far-fetched.

1089
00:41:38,039 --> 00:41:40,519
Just because Cao Jun knew he was the traitor back then,

1090
00:41:40,719 --> 00:41:41,800
he had to murder him?

1091
00:41:42,440 --> 00:41:43,000
Right.

1092
00:41:43,079 --> 00:41:44,760
If the fact that he was a traitor

1093
00:41:44,840 --> 00:41:46,000
really got exposed,

1094
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:48,480
a lot of veteran workers would curse him out.

1095
00:41:48,519 --> 00:41:49,920
But what real impact would that have on him?

1096
00:41:50,480 --> 00:41:51,800
He's just a retired old man

1097
00:41:52,000 --> 00:41:53,000
with a son and a grandson,

1098
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:54,039
living a happy, fulfilling life.

1099
00:41:54,159 --> 00:41:54,880
He'd commit murder

1100
00:41:56,920 --> 00:41:59,159
just out of fear that the past would come out

1101
00:41:59,639 --> 00:42:01,440
and ruin his reputation in his old age?

1102
00:42:03,239 --> 00:42:03,639
No way.

1103
00:42:03,920 --> 00:42:05,480
Is dignity really worth all that?

1104
00:42:06,440 --> 00:42:07,920
He doesn't strike me as that type.

1105
00:42:08,440 --> 00:42:09,960
There's definitely something deeper going on.

1106
00:42:10,360 --> 00:42:11,400
This case isn't over.

1107
00:42:18,840 --> 00:42:19,119
Seriously.

1108
00:42:19,119 --> 00:42:20,320
Who knows what else he was being blackmailed for?

1109
00:42:20,519 --> 00:42:20,960
Hello?

1110
00:42:21,559 --> 00:42:22,199
Officer Gao?

1111
00:42:22,199 --> 00:42:22,559
Hello.

1112
00:42:23,079 --> 00:42:25,039
I'm Cao Bing from the Xinbin scrapyard.

1113
00:42:25,480 --> 00:42:26,360
You came by earlier.

1114
00:42:26,880 --> 00:42:29,239
I... I have some information

1115
00:42:29,400 --> 00:42:30,199
I'd like to report to you.

1116
00:42:30,199 --> 00:42:30,960
Alright, wait for me there.

1117
00:42:30,960 --> 00:42:31,519
I'll be right over.

1118
00:42:44,519 --> 00:42:45,119
Go ahead.

1119
00:42:58,920 --> 00:42:59,760
Take photos, quick.

1120
00:43:04,159 --> 00:43:04,960
What's going on here?

1121
00:43:05,519 --> 00:43:07,679
Isn't this the car from Cao Jun's photo?

1122
00:43:08,039 --> 00:43:08,760
Last time I came,

1123
00:43:08,760 --> 00:43:09,760
you swore up and down

1124
00:43:09,760 --> 00:43:10,719
it wasn't at your factory.

1125
00:43:11,960 --> 00:43:14,480
Yeah. I didn't dare say it last time.

1126
00:43:16,639 --> 00:43:17,039
Alright.

1127
00:43:17,840 --> 00:43:19,320
Good thing you called me on your own.

1128
00:43:20,039 --> 00:43:21,079
When did this car get here?

1129
00:43:23,719 --> 00:43:24,639
Back around 2000.

1130
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:26,760
Over ten years, and it wasn't destroyed?

1131
00:43:26,760 --> 00:43:27,440
Why?

1132
00:43:35,599 --> 00:43:36,360
That night,

1133
00:43:36,559 --> 00:43:37,440
he was drunk driving.

1134
00:43:37,760 --> 00:43:39,639
He hit an out-of-town taxi.

1135
00:43:39,639 --> 00:43:40,679
What kind of taxi?

1136
00:43:40,679 --> 00:43:41,559
A red one.

1137
00:43:41,920 --> 00:43:42,920
The driver back then...

1138
00:43:43,519 --> 00:43:44,400
was still alive at the time.

1139
00:43:44,559 --> 00:43:45,840
He was going to kill me to keep me quiet.

1140
00:43:46,719 --> 00:43:48,480
I watched with my own eyes as Chen Qingchun

1141
00:43:48,599 --> 00:43:50,119
poured liquor down the driver's throat.

1142
00:43:51,280 --> 00:43:52,119
I wanted to save him,

1143
00:43:52,599 --> 00:43:53,320
but...

1144
